IMPORT prelude
IMPORT daydate
IMPORT `hda-types`
IMPORT `hda-flats`
IMPORT `hda-upgrading-board`

-- Housing and Development Act 1959 — THE TOP-LEVEL GOAL.
--
--   "For this HDB flat and its owner (or would-be owner), what does the Act
--    decide: may the person buy it; is this dealing with it lawful; is it
--    safe from creditors; and may the Board re-enter, compulsorily acquire
--    it, or impose a financial penalty instead?"
--
-- One answer through Part 4 (Goals 1-3). Upgrading (Goal 4), the Board
-- (Goal 5) and offences and service (Goal 6) answer their own questions in
-- `hda-upgrading-board.l4`.

§ `The top-level goal`

DECLARE `Flat position` HAS
    `entitled to purchase`                           IS A BOOLEAN
    `effect of the dealing`                          IS A MAYBE `Effect of a dealing`
    `protected from bankruptcy and attachment`       IS A BOOLEAN
    `does not vest in the Official Assignee on bankruptcy` IS A BOOLEAN
    `the Board may re-enter and determine the lease` IS A BOOLEAN
    `the Board may compulsorily acquire`             IS A BOOLEAN
    `most financial penalty instead of ss 50, 62 or 63` IS A MAYBE NUMBER

@ref ss 50, 52, 55, 56, 58, 59, 62, 63, 74
GIVEN f IS A `Flat case`
GIVETH A `Flat position`
`the flat position for` f MEANS
    `Flat position` WITH
        `entitled to purchase`                           IS `entitled to purchase a flat from the Board` (f's `purchase`)
        `effect of the dealing`                          IS
            CONSIDER f's `dealing`
            WHEN JUST d  THEN JUST (`the effect of` d)
            WHEN NOTHING THEN NOTHING
        `protected from bankruptcy and attachment`       IS `protected from bankruptcy and attachment, all owners non-citizens:` (f's `all owners are non-citizens`) `, a consented mortgagee or chargee enforcing:` FALSE
        `does not vest in the Official Assignee on bankruptcy` IS `does not vest in the Official Assignee on bankruptcy, all owners non-citizens:` (f's `all owners are non-citizens`)
        `the Board may re-enter and determine the lease` IS `the Board may re-enter and determine the lease` (f's `re-entry`)
        `the Board may compulsorily acquire`             IS `the Board may compulsorily acquire the flat on` (f's `acquisition grounds`)
        `most financial penalty instead of ss 50, 62 or 63` IS
            CONSIDER f's `a breach to be penalised instead, on`
            WHEN JUST b  THEN JUST (`the most financial penalty instead of ss 50, 62 or 63, breach on` b)
            WHEN NOTHING THEN NOTHING
